<title>USA: W. House sees Senate approval of Fed nominees soon.</title>
<headline>W. House sees Senate approval of Fed nominees soon.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House is hopeful that its two nominees to the Federal Reserve Board will be confirmed by the Senate soon, an official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect no problems,&quot; White House legislative affairs director John Hilley told Reuters Financial Television. &quot;We hope to have them in place very soon.&quot;</p>
<p>President Clinton earlier this month nominated University of Michigan professor Edward Gramlich and economic consultant Roger Ferguson to the central bank's board.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
